I agree with you that explore mode and wizard mode are there for trying 
out things: One for knowledge and the other for debuging[1].

But here we come to a major question:

Playing in explore mode is ok because you don't get recorded on 
highscore list. Are you suggesting that pudding farming would be ok if 
you don't get recorded on highscore list?

[1] One should use wizard mode cautiously for testing things as not all 
things work the same way in debugging mode as in normal play. Explore 
mode on the other hand does work like normal play except that one can 
decline dying. As it also guarantees an wand of wishing if you start in 
explore mode, I suggest that all testing. that can be done with a fully 
charged wand of wishing, should be conducted in explore mode so that we 
can be assured of the validity of the test.

